+// ─── B580.kext's xe connection, opened on this accelerator ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
+// Mesa ANV reaches the B580 through IOAccelB580Client (src/b580/B580Client.cpp; xemac opens it). On the B580 service
+// itself the system-graphics sandbox refuses it in every sandboxed Metal client (Safari, iconservicesagent,
+// VTDecoderXPCService, ...: system.sb allows iokit-open-user-client only with (iokit-connection "IOAccelerator")), and
+// the plugin then finds no Vulkan device. So the same client is handed out here: B580.kext creates it for the caller and
+// attaches and starts it on this accelerator ("b580NewClient"), so the service opened and the client's provider are
+// both this IOAccelerator, like the family's own clients. Its class and code stay in B580.kext (same external methods
+// and memory types); it holds a reference to the B580 service, B580.kext cannot unload while one is open, and this
+// accelerator's termination terminates it as any child. An older B580.kext answers kIOReturnUnsupported, and xemac
+// falls back to IOServiceOpen on B580.
+struct B580NewClient {   // B580Client.cpp, same layout
+    uint32_t version;    // 1
+    uint32_t type;
+    void *task, *securityID;
+    IOService *provider;
+    IOUserClient *client;
